---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section aria-labelledby="hero-title">
				<p>AI ENGINEERING · PLATFORM ENGINEERING · RELIABILITY</p>

				<h1 id="hero-title">Engineering AI for the real world.</h1>

				<p>
					I’m Ravikumar Buragapu, a Director of Engineering focused on
					AI engineering, platform engineering, and reliability at
					enterprise scale. I work on turning emerging technologies—from
					GenAI to agentic systems—into platforms that are secure,
					observable, resilient, and ready for production.
				</p>

				<p>
					My perspective is simple: the next phase of AI will be shaped
					not just by what models can do, but by how we engineer the
					systems around them—identity, evaluation, permissions,
					infrastructure, operational controls, and human accountability.
				</p>

				<p>
					<a href="/engineering">Explore engineering</a>
					·
					<a href="/writing">Read my writing</a>
					·
					<a href="/speak">Speaking</a>
				</p>
				<p>
					<a href="/projects/benchmarkkit">Explore BenchmarkKit, an open-source LLM and RAG benchmarking toolkit</a>
					·
					<a href="/projects/chief-of-staff">Explore Personal Chief of Staff, a multi-agent MCP assistant</a>
					·
					<a href="/projects/research-chat">Explore Chat with My Research, a citation-first RAG project</a>
					·
					<a href="/projects/learned-ann">Explore Learned ANN Index, a vector-search research prototype</a>
					·
					<a href="/projects/tokenizer-ablation">Explore Tokenizer Ablation, a from-scratch BPE and downstream study</a>
					·
					<a href="/projects/sequence-models">Explore RNN vs Transformer, a parameter-matched sequence study</a>
					·
					<a href="/projects/chunking-ablation">Explore Chunking Ablation, a controlled RAG retrieval study</a>
					·
					<a href="/projects/rag-judge-eval">Explore the Validated RAG Eval Harness, a human-vs-judge agreement study</a>
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="focus-title">
				<h2 id="focus-title">What I focus on</h2>

				<h3>AI and agentic systems</h3>
				<p>
					Designing the engineering foundations for production AI:
					agent identity, least-privilege access, evaluation,
					guardrails, observability, and controlled autonomy.
				</p>

				<h3>Platform engineering and developer productivity</h3>
				<p>
					Building platforms, reusable engineering capabilities,
					and automation that help teams deliver software faster
					while maintaining security, consistency, and quality.
				</p>

				<h3>Reliability and operational intelligence</h3>
				<p>
					Engineering resilient, data-intensive systems through
					observability, SRE practices, incident automation,
					capacity engineering, and measurable service objectives.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="experience-title">
				<h2 id="experience-title">Engineering leadership at scale</h2>

				<p>
					At Oracle Health, I lead engineering across infrastructure,
					reliability, and data intelligence platforms serving
					commercial, regulated, and Federal environments.
				</p>

				<p>
					Previously, at Wells Fargo, I formed the Agentic and GenAI
					Squad and helped shape agentic engineering strategy across
					an organization reaching more than 10,000 developers.
					At Adobe, I led platform engineering, the Agentic AI
					Builders Group, and development of an AI-driven
					Service Maturity Insights platform.
				</p>

				<p>
					My experience also includes engineering roles at Kohl’s
					and Charles Schwab, building on a software engineering
					career that began in India in 2000.
				</p>

				<p><a href="/about">More about my background and experience</a></p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="writing-title">
				<h2 id="writing-title">Ideas on engineering what comes next</h2>

				<p>
					I write about the engineering decisions that determine
					whether AI systems can be trusted in production—from
					evaluation and identity to governance, operational
					reliability, and the boundaries of agent autonomy.
				</p>

				<article>
					<h3>
						<a href="/blog/earning-agentic-autonomy">
							Earning Agentic Autonomy: An Eval Architecture for AI Agents
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p>
						How evaluation evidence, explicit controls, and
						runtime enforcement can help determine when an AI
						agent is ready to act with greater autonomy.
					</p>
				</article>

				<p><a href="/writing">Explore all articles</a></p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="connect-title">
				<h2 id="connect-title">Let's exchange ideas</h2>

				<p>
					I’m interested in conversations about production AI,
					agentic architectures, platform engineering, reliability,
					and the future of engineering organizations.
				</p>

				<p>
					<a href="/speak">Speaking and collaboration</a>
					·
					<a href="/about">About me</a>
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>